session:pr789Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #769 reported that literal_to_json (sparql_json.rs) encoded RdfLiteral::DurationLiteral with chrono::Duration's Debug impl ({:?}, e.g. 'TimeDelta { secs: 5, nanos: 0 }') instead of its Display impl, which is the valid ISO 8601 / xsd:duration lexical form -- breaking SPARQL JSON results conformance and preventing round-trip through from_sparql_json's parse_xsd_duration (added by #742). The issue asked to grep the serialize/ directory for the same {:?} pattern rather than fixing only the JSON call site, since bugs like this tend to be copy-pasted across the JSON/CSV/XML sibling serializers. That grep found the same bug independently in literal_to_csv (sparql_csv.rs) and literal_to_xml (sparql_xml.rs), but not in construct.rs's DurationLiteral arm, which already used Display correctly -- matching turtle/src/serialize.rs's existing pattern, confirming {} was the right fix rather than some other formatting. Followed TDD: added one regression test per affected serializer (ISO-8601-prefix assertion) plus a JSON round-trip test through from_sparql_json, confirmed all four failed with the literal Debug text as the panic message (red), then flipped {:?} to {} in all three sites and confirmed green. Also updated a stale doc comment in sparql_json.rs's parse_xsd_duration that had explicitly called out the Debug-vs-Display mismatch as 'not fixed here -- out of this issue's scope', since this PR is exactly that fix." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:789 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr789 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
